# .gitignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS FILE IS USED FOR:
# Tells GitHub which files/folders must NEVER be uploaded to the repository.
#
# - node_modules/ : hundreds of MB of downloaded packages; anyone can rebuild
#                   them with "npm install", so they are never committed.
# - .env          : contains the JWT secret, database password and Google
#                   client id. If it leaks, attackers can forge login tokens
#                   and access the database. It stays only on your machine;
#                   .env.example is the committed template instead.
# - *.log         : crash/debug logs are machine-local noise.
# - .DS_Store / Thumbs.db : OS junk files (macOS / Windows).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/
.env
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
